==================================================
WHY WE ARE CHANGING IT
==================================================

Current rigParts mixes two separate concepts:

STRUCTURE:

    mod
    parentIdx
    offsetX
    offsetY
    offsetZ
    scale

MOTION:

    animX
    animY
    animZ
    amplitude
    speed

This means:

- a part has one permanent motion definition
- there is no IDLE/WALK/ATTACK concept
- no phase offset
- changing action requires changing the skeleton data itself
- two legs with the same settings move in lockstep

We want:

    SKELETON
        stable hierarchy and transforms

    CLIPS
        named motion definitions

==================================================
IMPORTANT CORRECTION TO THE PROPOSED TRACK SHAPE
==================================================

Do NOT use only:

    {
      partIdx,
      axis,
      amplitude,
      speed,
      phase
    }

as the canonical track representation yet.

The existing rig allows a single part to animate X, Y and Z simultaneously:

    animX
    animY
    animZ

and generateRigBAS creates separate AX/AY/AZ accumulators and combines them in
one MODROT.

Therefore a safe migration must preserve multi-axis animation exactly.

Use:

    skeleton = {
      parts: [
        {
          id,
          label,
          mod,
          parentIdx,
          offsetX,
          offsetY,
          offsetZ,
          scale
        }
      ]
    }

    clips = [
      {
        id,
        name: "IDLE",
        loop: true,
        tracks: [
          {
            partIdx,
            x: {
              enabled,
              amplitude,
              speed,
              phase
            },
            y: {
              enabled,
              amplitude,
              speed,
              phase
            },
            z: {
              enabled,
              amplitude,
              speed,
              phase
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    ]

For PHASE 1:

    phase must default to 0
    and MUST NOT alter generated BAS yet.

We are storing it for the future only.

