==================================================
MIGRATION FROM CURRENT rigParts
==================================================

Create one explicit migration helper.

Something like:

    migrateLegacyRig(parts)

Input:

    existing rigParts[]

Output:

    {
      skeleton,
      clips
    }

For every old part:

STRUCTURE fields copy directly:

    mod
    parentIdx
    offsetX
    offsetY
    offsetZ
    scale
    label/id as applicable

MOTION becomes an IDLE track.

For each part:

    x.enabled = !!part.animX
    y.enabled = !!part.animY
    z.enabled = !!part.animZ

Current amplitude/speed are SHARED across enabled axes.

Therefore:

    enabled X -> x.amplitude = old amplitude
                 x.speed     = old speed

    enabled Y -> y.amplitude = old amplitude
                 y.speed     = old speed

    enabled Z -> z.amplitude = old amplitude
                 z.speed     = old speed

All phases:

    0

If no axis is enabled:

    either omit the track entirely

or

    retain it with all enabled=false

Prefer OMITTING empty tracks if that does not complicate later code.

Do not invent motion for static parts.

==================================================
DO NOT USE "NON-ZERO AMPLITUDE" AS THE MIGRATION TEST
==================================================

The design note suggested:

    one track per part that has a non-zero amplitude

That would be WRONG.

Current semantics explicitly use:

    amplitude = 0

to mean CONTINUOUS SPIN.

So amplitude 0 can absolutely be animated.

Animation existence is determined by:

    animX || animY || animZ

NOT amplitude > 0.

Preserve this exactly.

This is critical.

==================================================
CURRENT EXPORT SEMANTICS THAT MUST REMAIN IDENTICAL
==================================================

Today generateRigBAS does:

for each enabled axis:

    accumulator starts at 0

    AXn = AXn + speed
    AYn = AYn + speed
    AZn = AZn + speed

If amplitude == 0:

    continuous rotation:
        RAD(accumulator)

If amplitude > 0:

    sinusoidal swing:
        RAD(SIN(RAD(accumulator))*amplitude)

Then:

    MODROT n,rx,ry,rz

Structure remains:

    MODLOAD
    MODSET
    MODJOIN
    MODPOS

Do not change any of these semantics in PHASE 1.

